          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The
            %em flop transition
            is a continuous path in a space of
            %em noncommutative 2-geometries
            that starts at an ordinary complex 3-dimensional
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Calabi-Yau+space"} Calabi-Yau space
            = succeed ")" do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gepner+model"} Gepner point
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topology"} topology
          %p
            This was found and discussed in the context of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+theory"} string theory
            but the phenomenon is a general abstract one in the theory of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2d+SCFTs"} 2d SCFTs
            regarded as generalized geometries – as described at
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-spectral+triple"} 2-spectral triple
          %div{:style => "text-align: center"}
            %img{:src => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/FlopTransition.jpg", :width => "660"}/
          %blockquote
            %p
              graphics grabbed from
              %a{:href => "#Greene00"} Greene 00
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conifold+tansition"} conifold tansition
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+space+of+Calabi-Yau+spaces"} moduli space of Calabi-Yau spaces
          %h2#references References
          %p A survey is in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Brian+Greene"}> Brian Greene
              ,
              %em String Theory on Calabi-Yau Manifolds
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9702155"}> arXiv:hep-th/9702155
              )
          %p A rough and brief survey of the flop transition and related phenomena with many pointers to original literature is also given in
          %ul
            %li#Greene00
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Brian+Greene"}> Brian Greene
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Aspects of collapsing cocycles
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://www.theory.caltech.edu/~preskill/millennium.html"} Strings 2000
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://cdsweb.cern.ch/record/475955/files/0011059"} pdf
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1142/4599"} doi:10.1142/4599
          %p See also
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Shing-Tung+Yau"}> Shing-Tung Yau
              ,
              %em
                %a{:href => "http://www.scholarpedia.org/article/Calabi-Yau_manifold#Moduli_of_high_dimensional_Calabi-Yau_manifolds"} Moduli of high dimensional Calabi-Yau manifolds
          %p
            On the
            %span.newWikiWord
              quantum volume
              %a{:href => "/nlab/new/quantum+volume"} ?
            of vanishing cycles in the flop transition:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Brian+Greene"}> Brian Greene
                , Yakov Kanter,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Small Volumes in Compactified String Theory
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9612181"} arXiv:hep-th/9612181
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Brian+Greene"}> Brian Greene
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Calin+Lazaroiu"} Calin Lazaroiu
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Collapsing D-Branes in Calabi-Yau Moduli Space: I
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0001025"} arXiv:hep-th/0001025
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Calin+Lazaroiu"}> Calin Lazaroiu
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Collapsing D-branes in one-parameter models and small/large radius duality
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0002004"} arXiv:hep-th/0002004
            %li
              %p
                Mark Raugas,
                %em D-Branes and Vanishing Cycles in Higher Dimensions
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0102133"}> arXiv:hep-th/0102133
                )
